## 6. Calling a Project via URL

To execute/access a deployed project, the URL format is:

```
http://<IP-Address>:<Port>/<ProjectName>
```

| Component | Meaning | Example |
| --- | --- | --- |
| IP Address | Address of the server machine. When client and server are the same machine, use `localhost` | `localhost` |
| Port | Port number on which Tomcat listens (default) | `8080` |
| Project Name | Context path / project name deployed on the server | `J` |

**Example:**

```
http://localhost:8080/J
```

This calls the default `index.html` inside project `J`, and you should see output like **"Welcome to J"**.

> **Tip (from the video):** If you keep getting stale/old output even after changes, it's usually a **browser cache** issue — do a hard refresh (`Ctrl+Shift+R`), clear the cache, or open in a different browser/incognito window.
> 

