## 7. Creating an HTML Form (Front End)

**Goal:** Create a simple HTML form with a **Name** field and a **Submit** button.

```html
<!-- index.html -->
<html>
<body>
    <form>
        Name: <input type="text" name="name" placeholder="Enter your name">
        <input type="submit">
    </form>
</body>
</html>
```

### Logic:

- `<input type="text" name="name">` → takes user input, tagged with `name="name"` (this attribute is critical, it's how the backend will later retrieve the value).
- `<input type="submit">` → triggers form submission.
- Without an `action` attribute on `<form>`, clicking submit does **nothing** — you must tell the form **where to go** on submit.

