## 13. Common Errors & How to Debug Them

These are **very common real-world/interview scenarios**:

### Error 1: Invalid URL Pattern (Server fails to start)

```
Failed to start component ... Invalid <url-pattern> ... in servlet mapping
```

**Cause:** `url-pattern` does not start with `/`.
**Fix:** Always prefix URL patterns with `/`, e.g., `/callServlet` (not `callServlet`).

### Error 2: HTTP 404 Not Found

**Cause:** The form's `action` calls a Servlet name directly instead of going through `web.xml`'s URL pattern, or the URL pattern in `web.xml` doesn't match the form's `action`.
**Fix:** Ensure `action="..."` in the HTML **exactly matches** `<url-pattern>` in `web.xml`.

### Error 3: HTTP 500 — Internal Server Error / ClassNotFoundException

**Cause:** The `<servlet-class>` in `web.xml` doesn't include the **full package path**.

```xml
<!-- WRONG -->
<servlet-class>MyServlet</servlet-class>

<!-- CORRECT -->
<servlet-class>com.tap.MyServlet</servlet-class>
```

**Fix:** Always use the **fully qualified class name** (`package.ClassName`).

### General Debugging Tip

- Copy the exact error/stack trace and search it (e.g., on Stack Overflow or an AI assistant) — the **"Caused by:"** line in the stack trace usually points to the real root cause.
- **Restart the Tomcat server** after changing `web.xml`, since deployment descriptor changes often require a fresh server start to take effect.

